      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a get_file/fput pair in the C version of this driver around the next chunk, but I think it was actually cruft that failed to be removed, which is why we don\u0027t need it anymore:\n\nhttps://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/399360/\n\nI think I see how this happened, and it actually papered over a bug.\nOriginally, there was no `vma_set_file` helper, and the `ashmem` driver did:\n```\nget_file(asma-\u003efile)\nvma-\u003evm_file \u003d asma-\u003efile\n```\nworking with the condition that the `vma` didn\u0027t have a file in it before. This was to maintain the invariant that `vma` needs to have a ref to `vma-\u003evmfile`.\n\nThey also needed to `shmem_set_file`, which required a ref be held, so they put that in between the `get_file` and the `vma-\u003evmfile`.\n\nThey added the function `vma_set_file` which would incref the file going in, and decref any existing file. This means that instead of `vma-\u003evm_file \u003d asma-\u003efile` being the reference consumer, now an explicit `fput()` was added, because the `get_file()` needed to be held for `shmem_set_file`.\n\nFinally, `shmem_set_file` got replaced by `shmem_zero_setup`, and at this point, `get_file()` and `fput()` were not required, but the author didn\u0027t notice they could be removed.",
      "revId": "9c1edc5f6c78184931b0e832be3c320aafa93126",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
